+- For hand-authored or generated character animation, export one fixed-cell RGBA sprite sheet and a JSON manifest with top-left frame rectangles and FPS. Keep authored input frames as source art. Use a complete object as the cell for multi-tile props. Export an aligned normal sheet by default. The witch example is `assets/characters/witch-attack/` and is rebuilt with `.venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/build_witch_attack.py`.
 - Prefer 16x16 or 32x32 tiles, 32x64 or 64x128 character cells, RGBA PNG, a consistent palette, and nearest-neighbor scaling. Match any different dimensions explicitly requested by the user.
 - The default procedural generator has no per-call API cost. Use an image generation provider only when the requested art needs it; do not introduce billed API calls silently. `sprite-gen` is an optional reference workflow, not a dependency of the local generator.
 - When changing generator code, run `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m unittest discover -s tests -q`. For an asset change, verify image dimensions, alpha, and animation frame counts; inspect the visual result.
